{"label": "in~250", "t_monotonic": 22776.382171547, "t_monotonic_end": 22778.013635153, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "status": "ok", "http_status": 200, "first_token_ms": 1589.977486, "total_ms": 1631.39551, "tokens_in": 264, "tokens_out": 152, "reasoning_tokens": 7, "reasoning_text": "Need to give short paragraph.", "tokens_estimated": false, "text": "A B‑tree is a balanced, sorted multiway search tree in which each internal node can hold many keys and children, allowing data to be stored in large blocks that match disk pages. Because keys are kept in order and each node contains a range of keys, a B‑tree supports efficient range queries—retrieving all records between two values—by traversing a contiguous sequence of leaf nodes. Hash indexes, on the other hand, map keys to single buckets and do not preserve any ordering, making them unsuitable for range scans. Databases therefore favor B‑trees for queries that need to fetch contiguous ranges, while hash indexes are used only for exact‑match lookups.", "chunks": ["A", " B", "‑", "tree", " is", " a", " balanced", ",", " sorted", " multi", "way", " search", " tree", " in", " which", " each", " internal", " node", " can", " hold", " many", " keys", " and", " children", ",", " allowing", " data", " to", " be", " stored", " in", " large", " blocks", " that", " match", " disk", " pages", ".", " Because", " keys", " are", " kept", " in", " order", " and", " each", " node", " contains", " a", " range", " of", " keys", ",", " a", " B", "‑", "tree", " supports", " efficient", " range", " queries", "—", "retr", "ieving", " all", " records", " between", " two", " values", "—", "by", " travers", "ing", " a", " contiguous", " sequence", " of", " leaf", " nodes", ".", " Hash", " indexes", ",", " on", " the", " other", " hand", ",", " map", " keys", " to", " single", " buckets", " and", " do", " not", " preserve", " any", " ordering", ",", " making", " them", " unsuitable", " for", " range", " scans", ".", " Dat", "abases", " therefore", " favor", " B", "‑", "trees", " for", " queries", " that", " need", " to", " fetch", " contiguous", " ranges", ",", " while", " hash", " indexes", " are", " used", " only", " for", " exact", "‑", "match", " look", "ups", "."], "retry_after": null, "ratelimit_headers": {"rpd_limit": "1000", "tpm_limit": "8000", "rpd_remaining": "992", "tpm_remaining": "7549", "rpd_reset": "11m31.2s", "tpm_reset": "3.382s"}, "retries": 0, "max_tokens": 320, "finish_reason": "stop", "usage": {"queue_time": 0.809803751, "prompt_tokens": 264, "prompt_time": 0.126614694, "completion_tokens": 152, "completion_time": 0.185673528, "total_tokens": 416, "total_time": 0.312288222, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 7}}, "error_body": null, "headers": {"date": "Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:07:02 GMT", "content-type": "text/event-stream", "transfer-encoding": "chunked", "connection": "keep-alive", "cache-control": "no-cache", "server": "cloudflare", "vary": "Origin", "x-groq-region": "bom", "x-ratelimit-limit-requests": "1000", "x-ratelimit-limit-tokens": "8000", "x-ratelimit-remaining-requests": "992", "x-ratelimit-remaining-tokens": "7549", "x-ratelimit-reset-requests": "11m31.2s", "x-ratelimit-reset-tokens": "3.382s", "x-request-id": "req_01m77kk6r0etnafvsqdq001vw9", "via": "1.1 google", "set-cookie": "__cf_bm=QcgxfQb5gFwVpxsKG0lS7dOEKDxVFICjgNfMt6gFlHY-1794478021.3376915-1.0.1.1-ojpkwRx00boEvgDmiwhnLGU1e.qQghfO6Dv5D.gVzEHKp8X4CY8MjAJcdf8FkDukturFn30gS.G16nohfj6gSo0uXoeKM8jwQhQrSJ4ylQ5fW.YeOm1uIBAd97Y1XWOJ; HttpOnly; SameSite=None; Partitioned; Secure; Path=/; Domain=groq.com; Expires=Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:37:02 GMT", "strict-transport-security": "max-age=15552000", "cf-cache-status": "DYNAMIC", "cf-ray": "a594ba315ef2550c-DEL", "alt-svc": "h3=\":443\"; ma=86400"}}
{"label": "in~500", "t_monotonic": 22778.014557599, "t_monotonic_end": 22779.957313842, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "status": "ok", "http_status": 200, "first_token_ms": 1901.351483, "total_ms": 1942.661127, "tokens_in": 427, "tokens_out": 151, "reasoning_tokens": 5, "reasoning_text": "Need short paragraph.", "tokens_estimated": false, "text": "A B‑tree is a balanced, sorted tree data structure in which each node stores a small number of keys and child pointers. All leaf nodes are at the same depth, and the keys within each node are kept in sorted order, allowing efficient binary search inside a node. Databases use B‑trees rather than hash indexes for range queries because B‑trees maintain order across the entire data set: a range search can follow a path to the starting key and then sequentially traverse successive leaf nodes, yielding results in sorted order. A hash index, by contrast, only provides constant‑time lookups for exact keys and has no notion of key ordering, making range scans infeasible.", "chunks": ["A", " B", "‑", "tree", " is", " a", " balanced", ",", " sorted", " tree", " data", " structure", " in", " which", " each", " node", " stores", " a", " small", " number", " of", " keys", " and", " child", " pointers", ".", " All", " leaf", " nodes", " are", " at", " the", " same", " depth", ",", " and", " the", " keys", " within", " each", " node", " are", " kept", " in", " sorted", " order", ",", " allowing", " efficient", " binary", " search", " inside", " a", " node", ".", " Dat", "abases", " use", " B", "‑", "trees", " rather", " than", " hash", " indexes", " for", " range", " queries", " because", " B", "‑", "trees", " maintain", " order", " across", " the", " entire", " data", " set", ":", " a", " range", " search", " can", " follow", " a", " path", " to", " the", " starting", " key", " and", " then", " sequential", "ly", " traverse", " successive", " leaf", " nodes", ",", " yielding", " results", " in", " sorted", " order", ".", " A", " hash", " index", ",", " by", " contrast", ",", " only", " provides", " constant", "‑", "time", " look", "ups", " for", " exact", " keys", " and", " has", " no", " notion", " of", " key", " ordering", ",", " making", " range", " scans", " infe", "asible", "."], "retry_after": null, "ratelimit_headers": {"rpd_limit": "1000", "tpm_limit": "8000", "rpd_remaining": "991", "tpm_remaining": "7175", "rpd_reset": "12m57.599s", "tpm_reset": "6.187s"}, "retries": 0, "max_tokens": 320, "finish_reason": "stop", "usage": {"queue_time": 0.246461746, "prompt_tokens": 427, "prompt_time": 0.024466043, "completion_tokens": 151, "completion_time": 0.201559639, "total_tokens": 578, "total_time": 0.226025682, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 5}}, "error_body": null, "headers": {"date": "Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:07:03 GMT", "content-type": "text/event-stream", "transfer-encoding": "chunked", "connection": "keep-alive", "cache-control": "no-cache", "server": "cloudflare", "vary": "Origin", "x-groq-region": "bom", "x-ratelimit-limit-requests": "1000", "x-ratelimit-limit-tokens": "8000", "x-ratelimit-remaining-requests": "991", "x-ratelimit-remaining-tokens": "7175", "x-ratelimit-reset-requests": "12m57.599s", "x-ratelimit-reset-tokens": "6.187s", "x-request-id": "req_01m77kk889ed0r9yhtxkexmtmb", "via": "1.1 google", "cf-cache-status": "DYNAMIC", "set-cookie": "__cf_bm=jpWeXt7s2CxSUZVfg4S4SDU6Y4CCxvrNYmfiUtesIlk-1794478022.882651-1.0.1.1-rcda759ZLFangGS_sq_bha9Bz4hXN_eFZ4oFDvK8M.jJlOsHNDqyqP9nzT25xTWP_FyK79gwi0KdZf9Texp0boPRTo_vGolcVW0mp2L3qCInojnbkgm9LsMcxXey2t6B; HttpOnly; SameSite=None; Partitioned; Secure; Path=/; Domain=groq.com; Expires=Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:37:03 GMT", "strict-transport-security": "max-age=15552000", "cf-ray": "a594ba3b0b5451de-DEL", "alt-svc": "h3=\":443\"; ma=86400"}}
{"label": "in~1000", "t_monotonic": 22779.958043112, "t_monotonic_end": 22780.668299788, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "status": "ok", "http_status": 200, "first_token_ms": 672.76282, "total_ms": 710.14732, "tokens_in": 757, "tokens_out": 152, "reasoning_tokens": 5, "reasoning_text": "Need short paragraph.", "tokens_estimated": false, "text": "A B‑tree is a balanced, multi‑way search tree that stores keys in sorted order across its nodes, each node holding several keys and child pointers. Because the keys are kept in order, a B‑tree can efficiently traverse a contiguous range of values by following a single path from the first key to the last, retrieving all intermediate records in sequence. Databases prefer B‑trees over hash indexes for range queries because hash tables only support exact key lookups; they require a full table scan or additional indexing to answer “between” or “greater than” queries, whereas a B‑tree’s ordered structure allows range scans to be performed in logarithmic time with minimal I/O.", "chunks": ["A", " B", "‑", "tree", " is", " a", " balanced", ",", " multi", "‑", "way", " search", " tree", " that", " stores", " keys", " in", " sorted", " order", " across", " its", " nodes", ",", " each", " node", " holding", " several", " keys", " and", " child", " pointers", ".", " Because", " the", " keys", " are", " kept", " in", " order", ",", " a", " B", "‑", "tree", " can", " efficiently", " traverse", " a", " contiguous", " range", " of", " values", " by", " following", " a", " single", " path", " from", " the", " first", " key", " to", " the", " last", ",", " retrieving", " all", " intermediate", " records", " in", " sequence", ".", " Dat", "abases", " prefer", " B", "‑", "trees", " over", " hash", " indexes", " for", " range", " queries", " because", " hash", " tables", " only", " support", " exact", " key", " look", "ups", ";", " they", " require", " a", " full", " table", " scan", " or", " additional", " indexing", " to", " answer", " “", "bet