{"label": "in~2000", "t_monotonic": 22780.668977099, "t_monotonic_end": 22781.681511282, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "status": "ok", "http_status": 200, "first_token_ms": 985.373611, "total_ms": 1012.395869, "tokens_in": 1421, "tokens_out": 100, "reasoning_tokens": 5, "reasoning_text": "Need short paragraph.", "tokens_estimated": false, "text": "A B‑tree is a balanced, sorted multiway search tree in which each node can hold many keys and pointers, allowing efficient traversal with few disk accesses. Databases use B‑trees instead of hash indexes for range queries because B‑trees preserve key order, enabling contiguous scans of a key interval, while hash indexes only provide constant‑time equality lookups and require a full probe of the hash buckets to answer range conditions.", "chunks": ["A", " B", "‑", "tree", " is", " a", " balanced", ",", " sorted", " multi", "way", " search", " tree", " in", " which", " each", " node", " can", " hold", " many", " keys", " and", " pointers", ",", " allowing", " efficient", " traversal", " with", " few", " disk", " accesses", ".", " Dat", "abases", " use", " B", "‑", "trees", " instead", " of", " hash", " indexes", " for", " range", " queries", " because", " B", "‑", "trees", " preserve", " key", " order", ",", " enabling", " contiguous", " scans", " of", " a", " key", " interval", ",", " while", " hash", " indexes", " only", " provide", " constant", "‑", "time", " equality", " look", "ups", " and", " require", " a", " full", " probe", " of", " the", " hash", " buckets", " to", " answer", " range", " conditions", "."], "retry_after": null, "ratelimit_headers": {"rpd_limit": "1000", "tpm_limit": "8000", "rpd_remaining": "989", "tpm_remaining": "5034", "rpd_reset": "15m50.4s", "tpm_reset": "22.245s"}, "retries": 0, "max_tokens": 320, "finish_reason": "stop", "usage": {"queue_time": 0.446519804, "prompt_tokens": 1421, "prompt_time": 0.14323868, "completion_tokens": 100, "completion_time": 0.112932149, "total_tokens": 1521, "total_